```python
def dfs(graph, node, visited=None):
    if visited is None:
        visited = set()
    visited.add(node)
    for neighbor in graph[node]:
        if neighbor not in visited:
            dfs(graph, neighbor, visited)
    return visited
```

content:
Simple Python implementation of Graph depth-first search

This came up in code review a few times, so here's the version we settled on.

```python
def dfs(graph, node, visited=None):
    if visited is None:
        visited = set()
    visited.add(node)
    for neighbor in graph[node]:
        if neighbor not in visited:
            dfs(graph, neighbor, visited)
    return visited
```

