This came up in code review a few times, so here's the version we settled on.

```javascript
async function callWithBackoff(fn, retries = 5, baseDelay = 500) {
  for (let attempt = 0; attempt < retries; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempt === retries - 1) throw err;
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, baseDelay * 2 ** attempt));
    }
  }
}
```

