body:
Sharing our internal standard for this pattern so new hires have something to copy from.

```javascript
function throttle(fn, limit) {
  let inThrottle;
  return (...args) => {
    if (!inThrottle) {
      fn(...args);
      inThrottle = true;
      setTimeout(() => (inThrottle = false), limit);
    }
  };
}
```

content:
JavaScript example: Throttle function

Sharing our internal standard for this pattern so new hires have something to copy from.

```javascript
function throttle(fn, limit) {
  let inThrottle;
  return (...args) => {
    if (!inThrottle) {
      fn(...args);
      inThrottle = true;
      setTimeout(() => (inThrottle = false), limit);
    }
  };
}
```

--- Accepted Answer ---
We added tests for the edge cases (empty input, single element) separately.

